# Dev Variant Presenter

**Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root.** It is the single source of truth for how to work here:
architecture, starting and stopping the server, fresh-clone setup, and tests. This rule file exists
only so Cursor always has the two critical constraints loaded; everything else lives in `AGENTS.md`
so there is one copy to keep correct.

- **Start the server ONLY via the watchdog** — `run_server.ps1` on Windows, `run_server.sh` on
  Linux/macOS. Never bare `python -m dev_variant_presenter`, and never a generic preview or
  dev-server launcher. Those skip the watchdog, so a routine ovrtx/ovstream native crash becomes a
  dead app with no relaunch and no logs.
- **The stream is single-client.** Opening a second browser or client steals the active session.

Full step-by-step procedures are in `.claude/skills/start-server/SKILL.md` and
`.claude/skills/setup-environment/SKILL.md`. They are plain Markdown — read them by path.
